  era: "c. 300 BCE\u2013300 CE \xB7 Section 9 \xB7 Sangam Age \xB7 c. 3rd century BCE \u2013 3rd century CE"
  title: Sangam literature
  text: Sangam literature is the earliest Tamil poetry, composed roughly between the 3rd century BCE and the 3rd century CE, traditionally at assemblies, or sangams, in Madurai. Its poems of love, called akam, and of war and public life, called puram, fill anthologies such as Ettuthokai and Pattuppattu. Tolkappiyam is its grammar.
